* dit_imm -- deferred INDIRECT-REFERENCE as an IMMEDIATE-assignment ($) capture target.
* ORACLE (sbl -bf): "ok dummy=HELLO" -- the assignment lands.
* SCRIP: "ok dummy=" -- the match succeeds but the assignment is SILENTLY DROPPED.
* ⛔ This arm is worse than dit_cond: a wrong answer with no failure signal.
	subject = "HELLO WORLD"
	p = "HELLO" $ *$("dummy")
	subject p	:S(ok)F(no)
ok	OUTPUT = "ok dummy=" dummy	:(END)
no	OUTPUT = "failed"
END
